window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c96f1de8b434cae9"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"draft-prds-from-internal-context\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"prd\">根据内部背景资料起草 PRD</h1> <p>根据 Linear、Slack、来源文档和会议笔记创建产品需求文档。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT、$documents 技能以及 Linear、Slack、Notion 或 Google Drive 等已连接的插件，创建可供检查的 PRD，包含预期章节、时间线、决策、待解决问题和 来源附录。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>将规划背景资料整理成 PRD、提案、发布简报或决策备忘录的产品团队。</li> <li>在团队通过内部讨论达成共识后，需要快速起草 PRD 的产品经理。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>当 PRD 需要成为排版完善的文件，而不只是聊天文本时，创建、编辑并 验证 DOCX。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>从经批准的频道或讨论串链接中，读取产品讨论、发布讨论串、决策记录 和后续问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取应纳入 PRD 的项目、问题、优先级、验收标准和未完成工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取规划文档、研究笔记、规格说明、导出的会议笔记和来源文件夹。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/notion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">notion（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取应纳入 PRD 的路线图页面、项目笔记、会议笔记和团队维基。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>起草 PRD</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $documents，为 [feature or product area] 创建一份 PRD，来源是 @linear [project or milestone]、@slack [channel or thread]，以及 @google-drive 或 @notion [planning docs, research notes, meeting notes, or source folder]。\n\n包含问题、用户、目标与非目标、需求、UX、技术考虑、指标、发布计划、风险、 待解决问题、决策、时间线和来源附录。\n\n对需求层面的陈述引用其依据来源。如果来源之间存在分歧，请指出冲突，而不是 默默选择其中一种说法。仅起草；在我批准之前，不要发布、更新 Linear 或分享文档。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent 技能</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾加上 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>开始开发新产品或功能前，通常会起草一份产品需求文档（PRD），让大家对范围和需求形成共识。撰写 PRD 所需的背景资料往往已经存在于团队内部系统中，例如 Linear 上的问题单、Slack 中的讨论，以及 Notion 或 Google Drive 里的草稿。ChatGPT 可以收集这些资料并起草一份 PRD，供你检查和迭代，同时清楚保留来源线索。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-sources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">选择来源</h2> <p>先明确你希望 ChatGPT 使用哪些来源：Linear 项目、Slack 的规划频道或讨论串，以及 PRD 应引用的 Drive 文档、Notion 页面、会议笔记或本地文件。 你还应明确列出预期的 PRD 章节，例如问题、用户、需求、UX、技术、发布计划、时间线或决策。</p> <ol> <li>如果输出应是一份真正的 DOCX，先使用 <code>$documents</code>。</li> <li>直接指明来源：Linear 项目或里程碑、Slack 频道或讨论串，以及 ChatGPT 应引用的文档或笔记。</li> <li>向 ChatGPT 明确约定 PRD 的章节要求。</li> <li>先检查来源附录，再检查需求和待解决问题。</li> <li>在同一个聊天中填补缺口、收紧范围，并准备交接。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"refine-in-the-same-chat\"></a> <a id=\"refine-in-the-same-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">在同一个聊天中完善</h2> <p>起草第一版时，可以使用本页的起步提示词。如果缺少内容，请将缺失的来源提供给 ChatGPT，而不是从头开始。</p> <p><a id=\"check-the-source-trail\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">检查来源线索</h2> <p>分享 PRD 前，请 ChatGPT 列出缺乏充分依据或没有来源支持的陈述、未解决的问题，以及它视为已确认的决策。如果来源附录不能让这些内容易于核查，请继续在同一个聊天中完善，再导出或发布任何内容。</p> <p><a id=\"suggested-prompt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">建议提示词</h3> <p><strong>检查来源线索</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Before I share this PRD, check the source trail.\n\nList:\n\n- requirements with weak or missing source support\n- open questions that still need an owner or decision\n- decisions you treated as confirmed\n- any claims that should move out of the PRD and into open questions\n\nKeep the source appendix linked and easy to audit.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">在我分享这份产品需求文档（PRD）之前，请检查来源链。\n\n列出：\n\n- 来源支持薄弱或缺失的需求\n- 仍需负责人或决策的待解答问题\n- 你视为已经确认的决定\n- 应从 PRD 移到待解答问题中的主张\n\n保留来源附录的链接，并让其便于审查。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"draft-prds-from-internal-context\">Draft PRDs from internal context</h1> <p>Create product requirements documents from Linear, Slack, source documents, and meeting notes.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with the $documents skill and connected plugins such as Linear, Slack, Notion or Google Drive to create a reviewable PRD with the expected sections, a timeline, decisions, open questions, and a source appendix.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Product teams turning planning context into a PRD, proposal, launch brief, or decision memo.</li> <li>PMs who need to draft a PRD quickly after aligning with the team in internal discussions.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Create, edit, and verify a DOCX when the PRD should become a polished file instead of chat text.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read product discussions, launch threads, decision notes, and follow-up questions from approved channels or thread links.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear (online)</a></td> <td>Read projects, issues, priorities, acceptance criteria, and open work that should shape the PRD.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read planning docs, research notes, specs, exported meeting notes, and source folders.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/notion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">notion (online)</a></td> <td>Read roadmap pages, project notes, meeting notes, and team wikis that should shape the PRD.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Draft the PRD</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $documents to create a PRD for [feature or product area] from @linear [project or milestone], @slack [channel or thread], and @google-drive or @notion [planning docs, research notes, meeting notes, or source folder].\n\nInclude the problem, users, goals/non-goals, requirements, UX, technical considerations, metrics, launch plan, risks, open questions, decisions, timeline, and source appendix.\n\nCite the sources behind requirement-level claims. If sources disagree, call out the conflict instead of choosing silently. Draft only. Do not post, update Linear, or share the document until I approve it.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Before working on a new product or feature, it's common to draft a product requirements document (PRD) to align on the scope and requirements. Most often than not, the context needed to write that PRD is already available in the team's internal systems: tickets on Linear, discussions on Slack, drafts in Notion or Google Drive, etc. ChatGPT can gather this context and draft a PRD that you can review and iterate on, while keeping the source trail visible.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-sources\">Choose the sources</h2> <p>Start with the sources you want ChatGPT to use: the Linear project, the Slack planning channel or thread, and any Drive docs, Notion pages, meeting notes, or local files that should be cited in the PRD. You should also clearly outline the PRD sections you expect, such as the problem, users, requirements, UX, tech, launch plan, timeline, or decisions.</p> <ol> <li>Start with <code>$documents</code> when the output should be a real DOCX.</li> <li>Name the sources directly: the Linear project or milestone, the Slack channel or thread, and the docs or notes ChatGPT should cite.</li> <li>Give ChatGPT the PRD section contract.</li> <li>Review the source appendix first, then the requirements and open questions.</li> <li>Use the same chat to resolve gaps, tighten scope, and prepare the handoff.</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"refine-in-the-same-chat\"></a> <a id=\"refine-in-the-same-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"refine-in-the-same-chat\">Refine in the same chat</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt on this page for the first draft. If something is missing, point ChatGPT at the missing source instead of starting over.</p> <h2 id=\"check-the-source-trail\">Check the source trail</h2> <p>Before sharing the PRD, ask ChatGPT to list the claims with weak or missing support, the unresolved questions, and the decisions it treated as confirmed. If the source appendix does not make those easy to audit, keep refining the same chat before exporting or posting anything.</p> <h3 id=\"suggested-prompt\">Suggested prompt</h3> <p><strong>Check the Source Trail</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Before I share this PRD, check the source trail.\n\nList:\n\n- requirements with weak or missing source support\n- open questions that still need an owner or decision\n- decisions you treated as confirmed\n- any claims that should move out of the PRD and into open questions\n\nKeep the source appendix linked and easy to audit.\n</code></pre>"};
